# What NOT to send to the builder.
#
# Two images build from the repository ROOT (images/operator, images/slapd-
# exporter), so without this the whole working tree travels to the worker on
# every build -- which with a remote BuildKit worker is a network transfer,
# not a local copy. A developer tree here is multiple GB of build output and
# tooling state against ~9 MB of tracked source.
#
# BuildKit reads .dockerignore ONLY. podman also honoured .containerignore, so
# a file by that name would be silently ignored now -- the failure mode being
# a slow build rather than a broken one, which is why it would not get noticed.
#
# Keep this an exclude list rather than an allow list: both Containerfiles
# COPY one module directory each, so anything not excluded costs transfer and
# nothing else, while an allow list that forgets a new source directory breaks
# the build.

# Version control and build state
.git
.github
.gitea
.stamps
.build
.charts
bin/
dist/

# Agent/editor/tooling state
.claude
.idea
.vscode

# Go build output and module caches that may sit in-tree
operator/bin/
exporter/bin/
**/*.test

# Nothing below is reachable from either Containerfile's COPY, and all of it
# is large or noisy.
docs/
charts/
monitoring/
tests/
images/
scripts/
*.log
*.tar
*.tgz
